  "schema": "ra3-a3r-asymmetry-v1",
  "theorem": "fragment_hex (exact.f1_normal_form) can be non-None at a point of a walk only if an earlier joint in the same walk already abandoned a hexagon. F<=1 allows at most one abandonment total. So if a word's SECOND event is itself abandoning (RA2, RA3), no earlier abandonment (visible or the hidden zero-charge Z2_abandon_w2_new) can have fired -- fragment_hex is forced None at every point up to and including just before that second event. This is a deductive consequence of the model's F<=1 constraint, not an empirical regularity."
